# Which built image every NAME resolves to. One file, so a version bump is one edit.
#
# The problem this exists to stop: nothing pointed at an image by role, so every consumer spelled
# a version. 169 campaign .env files still say hpcagent-bench-amd-mi300-v4 and canon_column.sh says v5,
# which is not a decision anyone made -- it is where each file happened to stop being edited. A
# results table then cites an EDF name that means a different image depending on when it was run.
#
# So: consumers name LATEST, this file says what latest is, and promotion is a one-line change
# here followed by install_edfs.sh. Nothing names a version -- see below, there are none left to
# name, and a run that spells one silently opts out of every fix promoted after it was written.
#
# The DIGEST remains the identity of a build. LATEST is a convenience for launching, never the
# thing a results table quotes; build.sh writes <sqsh>.digest for that.

# ONE VERSION PER ROLE. Every name here is unversioned and every rebuild replaces it, so there is
# never a v2 and a v8 to reconcile: the .sqsh basename says which image it is and the .digest says
# which build. A build writes <role>-candidate.sqsh and build.sbatch refuses to write over an image
# an EDF mounts, so promotion is verify-then-rename and a running arm never reads a half-written
# squashfs.
#
# What this gives up, deliberately: there is no version to pin a run to. A results table cites the
# DIGEST, which was always the identity anyway -- a moving tag over two different images is what
# made citing one meaningless.

# Judge + agent. On beverin ONE image serves both the CPU arms and the GPU arms -- the GPU entries
# below are inference engines, not a second judge image. The CPU-only pair further down is for a host
# with no AMD toolchain at all, not a second beverin build.
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_SQSH="hpcagent-bench-agent-mi300.sqsh"
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-agent-mi300-latest"
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_TEMPLATE="judge-agent-amd/edf.toml.example"

# The JUDGE role, split out 2026-09-09. It is the agent image plus hpcagent_bench, built as a
# second --target of the SAME Dockerfile, so the two cannot drift and building both costs one
# agent build plus a pip layer.
#
# Why it is a separate image at all: installing hpcagent_bench ships hpcagent_bench/benchmarks --
# 3850 reference files the agents are graded against -- so a single fused image cannot both give
# the judge the library and keep it from the agents. The judge stage carries the
# trusted-judge-image firewall marker; held-out hidden_tests stay out of BOTH images and are read
# from the host mount.
JUDGE_AMD_SQSH="hpcagent-bench-judge-mi300.sqsh"
JUDGE_AMD_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-judge-mi300-latest"
JUDGE_AMD_TEMPLATE="judge-agent-amd/edf.judge.toml.example"

# The RELEASE judge: the saved agent archive plus hpcagent_bench at one git ref, built by
# judge-agent-amd/build-judge-release.sh in ~30 min on a login node. Runs do not use it -- they mount
# the checkout (run_cluster.sh puts it first on PYTHONPATH) -- it exists to be PUBLISHED, tagged with
# the git sha it carries. A candidate name, so it can never land on a name an EDF mounts.
JUDGE_AMD_RELEASE_SQSH="hpcagent-bench-judge-mi300-release-candidate.sqsh"

# The judge + agent pair for partition mi200 (MI250X gfx90a, EPYC 7A53 Zen 3): the same Dockerfile
# and templates, built ON mi200 with ROCM_ARCH from gpu_arch.env and spack target zen3 from
# cpu_target.env. The mi300 images cannot run there: their zen4 spack stack (mimalloc preloaded
# into every process) dies on SIGILL at container start. Smoke tests only -- mi200 numbers are
# never paper data. The -mlscale EDF is the judge EDF plus the libhwloc.so.15 preload multi-node
# MPI_Init needs, as hpcagent-bench-judge-mi300-mlscale is for mi300.
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_MI200_SQSH="hpcagent-bench-agent-mi200.sqsh"
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_MI200_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-agent-mi200-latest"
JUDGE_AMD_MI200_SQSH="hpcagent-bench-judge-mi200.sqsh"
JUDGE_AMD_MI200_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-judge-mi200-latest"
JUDGE_AMD_MI200_MLSCALE_EDF="hpcagent-bench-judge-mi200-mlscale"

# Inference, the two engines campaigns mount: sglang serves qwen38 and kimi, vllm serves oss120b
# because the mxfp4 path gpt-oss needs is what its 0.23.0 has.
#
# Both now name an image this repo builds from a single Dockerfile. Until 2026-09-08 they named
# upstream pulls produced by a multi-phase chain, and what sglang/Dockerfile and vllm/Dockerfile
# build had never been promoted into service. That is why the sglang arms still carried
# PYTHONPATH=${SCRATCH}/pyprefix for cupy and flydsl: the served image did not have them. The
# pulls also carried a squashfs sha256 and no .digest, so publishing one published something the
# repo could not rebuild. They were deleted on 2026-09-08 along with their EDFs.
INFERENCE_SGLANG_SQSH="${INFERENCE_SGLANG_SQSH:-hpcagent-bench-sglang-mi300.sqsh}"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-sglang-mi300-latest"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_TEMPLATE="sglang/edf.toml.example"
INFERENCE_VLLM_SQSH="${INFERENCE_VLLM_SQSH:-hpcagent-bench-vllm-mi300.sqsh}"
INFERENCE_VLLM_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-vllm-mi300-latest"
INFERENCE_VLLM_TEMPLATE="vllm/edf.toml.example"

# SGLang for partition mi200 (MI250X, gfx90a). Its own image: sgl_kernel and cupy carry per-arch
# device code and aiter has no gfx90a kernels. See sglang-mi200/README.md.
INFERENCE_SGLANG_MI200_SQSH="${INFERENCE_SGLANG_MI200_SQSH:-hpcagent-bench-sglang-mi200.sqsh}"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_MI200_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-sglang-mi200-latest"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_MI200_TEMPLATE="sglang-mi200/edf.toml.example"

# GH200 (CSCS Daint: aarch64 Grace + H100 96 GB, 4 per node). Built, promoted and rendered ON
# Daint, never on beverin -- README.md "Daint (GH200)". install_edfs.sh renders these three only with
# CE_PLATFORM=gh200, so a beverin checkout without the images installs exactly what it always did.
# judge-agent-cuda is two targets like judge-agent-amd: the agent image carries no hpcagent_bench.
# One engine for every model there: the official vLLM image, pinned by digest in vllm-cuda/Dockerfile.
JUDGE_AGENT_CUDA_SQSH="hpcagent-bench-agent-gh200.sqsh"
JUDGE_AGENT_CUDA_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-agent-gh200-latest"
JUDGE_AGENT_CUDA_TEMPLATE="judge-agent-cuda/edf.toml.example"
JUDGE_CUDA_SQSH="hpcagent-bench-judge-gh200.sqsh"
JUDGE_CUDA_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-judge-gh200-latest"
JUDGE_CUDA_TEMPLATE="judge-agent-cuda/edf.judge.toml.example"
INFERENCE_VLLM_CUDA_SQSH="${INFERENCE_VLLM_CUDA_SQSH:-hpcagent-bench-vllm-gh200.sqsh}"
INFERENCE_VLLM_CUDA_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-vllm-gh200-latest"
INFERENCE_VLLM_CUDA_TEMPLATE="vllm-cuda/edf.toml.example"

# CPU only, lightweight, on whichever architecture builds it -- so every name carries that
# architecture: an x86_64 and an aarch64 build on one scratch (or one ~/.edf) never overwrite each
# other. Rendered by install_edfs.sh with CE_PLATFORM=cpu.
JUDGE_AGENT_CPU_SQSH="hpcagent-bench-agent-cpu-$(uname -m).sqsh"
JUDGE_AGENT_CPU_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-agent-cpu-$(uname -m)-latest"
JUDGE_AGENT_CPU_TEMPLATE="judge-agent-cpu/edf.toml.example"
JUDGE_CPU_SQSH="hpcagent-bench-judge-cpu-$(uname -m).sqsh"
JUDGE_CPU_EDF_LATEST="hpcagent-bench-judge-cpu-$(uname -m)-latest"
JUDGE_CPU_TEMPLATE="judge-agent-cpu/edf.judge.toml.example"

# vLLM 0.27.1 was RETIRED on 2026-09-08 and lives on the parked/vllm-0271 branch. Measured on one
# pinned node, same probe and parsers, it served oss120b at 2405 tok/s against 0.23.0's 3013 --
# 25% slower, and the gap is entirely in decode (steady-state 2540 vs 3187 tok/s; prefill matched
# to 0.3%). Same dtype, quantization, MoE and attention backends, same torch and triton, so it was
# vLLM's own decode path. Restore the branch rather than re-deriving this.

# PROMOTION: build to <role>-candidate.sqsh with build_and_verify.sbatch, then
#
#     ./promote_image.sh --all            (DRY_RUN=1 to see what would move)
#
# which renames the candidate over the live name above, carries the .digest, .sha256 and .oci.tar
# sidecars with it, and re-runs install_edfs.sh with ALLOW_REPOINT=1. It REFUSES a candidate with
# no .verified marker, which only a clean build_and_verify verdict writes.
#
# The rename is safe while arms are running -- a mounted squashfs is held by its inode, so a job
# that already started keeps reading the bytes it opened and only new jobs see the new image.
#
# The sidecars must move WITH the image. They are the only record of WHICH build a name currently
# holds, and with one version per role there is nothing else to tell two apart.

# Registry: ONE repository for every image -- https://hub.docker.com/r/spcleth/hpcagent-bench
#
# TAGS ARE AN EXPLICIT MAP, not derived from the .sqsh basename. They used to be computed as
# `basename minus the hpcagent-bench- prefix`, which produced ce-amd-mi300, ce-judge-amd-mi300, sglang
# and vllm. NONE of those four tags exist on the hub -- every one returns 404 -- so
# pull_images.sbatch, documented in the README as "THE DEFAULT WAY to get images", could not
# fetch a single role. A derived tag silently desynchronises from what was actually pushed; a map
# is checked by reading it. (Verified against the registry 2026-09-16.)
#
# NAMING, and why the tag carries the target. One repository holds every role, so the TAG IS THE
# ONLY NAMESPACE. This repo also builds judge-agent-cuda and sglang-mi200; the moment either is
# published, a bare `agent-latest` or `hpcagent-bench-sglang-mi300-latest` collides with it. So the target scheme is
# <role>-<target>-latest, e.g. agent-mi300-latest.
#
# The hub does not carry those tags yet -- publishing them needs registry write access, which is
# not available from the cluster. Until then CURRENT_TAG below holds what is actually published
# and TARGET_TAG records where it is going: when you can push, run push_image.sh to publish the
# target names and move each CURRENT_TAG onto its TARGET_TAG. One edit per role, here.
#
# These tags MOVE, one per role. push_image.sh publishes a sha-<digest> tag alongside each, and a
# dated <role>-<YYYYMMDD>; cite one of those in a results table, never the moving one.
REGISTRY_REPO="${REGISTRY_REPO:-docker.io/spcleth/hpcagent-bench}"
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_REPO="${REGISTRY_REPO}"
JUDGE_AMD_REPO="${REGISTRY_REPO}"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_REPO="${REGISTRY_REPO}"
INFERENCE_VLLM_REPO="${REGISTRY_REPO}"

# A REGISTRY TAG IS NOT AN EDF NAME. They look alike and they are not interchangeable: a tag
# names bytes in a repository, an EDF names a rendered file in ~/.edf. A blanket rename that
# rewrote EDF names across the tree also rewrote these two, and the pull asked the registry
# for "hpcagent-bench-vllm-mi300-latest" -- 404, because no such tag was ever pushed.
# tests/test_registry_tags_are_not_edf_names.py keeps the two namespaces apart.
#                              published now          where it is going
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_TAG="${JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_TAG:-agent-latest}"
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_TAG_TARGET="agent-mi300-latest"
JUDGE_AMD_TAG="${JUDGE_AMD_TAG:-judge-latest}"
JUDGE_AMD_TAG_TARGET="judge-mi300-latest"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_TAG="${INFERENCE_SGLANG_TAG:-sglang-latest}"
INFERENCE_SGLANG_TAG_TARGET="sglang-mi300-latest"
INFERENCE_VLLM_TAG="${INFERENCE_VLLM_TAG:-vllm-latest}"
INFERENCE_VLLM_TAG_TARGET="vllm-mi300-latest"
# Not published yet; push_image.sh --from-archive publishes them under these names.
JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_MI200_TAG="${JUDGE_AGENT_AMD_MI200_TAG:-agent-mi200-latest}"
JUDGE_AMD_MI200_TAG="${JUDGE_AMD_MI200_TAG:-judge-mi200-latest}"
# The release judge has no moving tag of its own: it is published as judge-mi300-<git sha12>, which
# build-judge-release.sh prints, and push_images.sbatch refuses the role until this is set.
JUDGE_AMD_RELEASE_TAG="${JUDGE_AMD_RELEASE_TAG:-}"

# GETTING THE IMAGES: pull is the DEFAULT, build is the option.
#
# A rebuild is one node for hours -- the judge+agent image bootstraps gcc 16 and then llvm 22
# before it reaches PETSc and MAGMA. A pull is bandwidth, and it gets the SAME BYTES rather than a
# new build that happens to share a Dockerfile. For anyone reproducing this work, that difference
# is the whole point: the digest they cite is the digest we published.
#
#   sbatch containers/cluster/ce-images/pull_images.sbatch          # all four roles
#   ./pull_image.sh judge-agent-amd sha-<digest>                    # one, pinned
#
# Build when you are CHANGING an image, or when a role has not been published yet:
#
#   IMAGE_DIR=$PWD/judge-agent-amd sbatch build_and_verify.sbatch
